#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937} :activity/id #uuid "6e7bba4e-e339-5059-bc4b-363cbe14a29f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90d6f3fc-4b07-573d-909e-71ad76038bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113918} {:answer/id #uuid "66d8f448-8728-5a93-9a65-75b7c8a60923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2+3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492423} {:answer/id #uuid "8de04b4a-cc0c-503c-b014-8f1ba934eb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} {:answer/id #uuid "977e4b58-8b63-5c8e-b09e-907ea3fc4715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492510} {:answer/id #uuid "b58da9b9-82d8-54d2-94d7-4d4f9a370f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-3z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c202514-58b0-57fd-9d4a-d9d9f27c390e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8cd9c6c5-780e-5f01-93cc-d5e9b9533129" :question/math-academy-id "q-42040" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=-2 \\\\ x+y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=-2 \\\\ y-3z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-3z \\\\ y=2+3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2361ed3b-bfae-5a29-916a-e207bd92ed86" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c122c68-ba85-506a-9b5d-b7e8d41f11b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492400} {:answer/id #uuid "90746f9d-5a52-5223-86f2-eebad7cce602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492502} {:answer/id #uuid "a00e12c1-efd1-5bb1-8807-973d94c98793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492536} {:answer/id #uuid "af7e5af6-3e33-5368-823c-3062f7002694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492568} {:answer/id #uuid "fcccf2b5-4696-5f4a-92c9-3b29f694860e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492701}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492568} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ab4b9b-dc34-5dc7-8a1e-ba7fb0076d92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "22d64530-5ce7-515c-aafe-c528e2fc812f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74834" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-7y=0 \\\\  & -4x+15y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=2$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=7.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} :step/id #uuid "49cc5d2d-b51f-5454-b5d2-2fecc8135eb1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14622e0-0a8b-52f6-8bf8-44a04ea90e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} {:answer/id #uuid "422e0298-fb2d-5c6d-a4af-8cba072754ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddef766-7f45-5b44-b48d-737353d4be25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522be474-9268-5719-9b67-fa3c52635318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437898} {:answer/id #uuid "37b81bb5-685b-583b-8db4-0245d173fc7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b79b55-bd9c-5274-8736-1fa18bb4e7d7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63da7652-c50c-579a-9313-44ed8eac188b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} {:answer/id #uuid "715c6b27-3b25-5248-a7ad-aceb0fe78ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} :answer-field/id #uuid "a893b756-f994-5e2f-ab56-a98d5a543109" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131722" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system has no solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} :step/id #uuid "4f6ca757-aec4-527a-86a3-ce82de0d867c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7b0d87-9712-510c-adb7-5bde077204da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492235} {:answer/id #uuid "58ea3fc2-519f-5eea-8c33-6dce5b9c6e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492389} {:answer/id #uuid "8133480e-57da-5ca9-9bce-a1b99fc82856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492477} {:answer/id #uuid "a85d27da-01e0-5767-a1e4-b5479a5241b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492558} {:answer/id #uuid "da15d75f-b174-5630-b7ee-c26933c1301a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492646}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492477} :answer-field/id #uuid "df2effb2-e366-52f0-a14b-bc202d0cbc2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7409a043-b196-5341-8318-5b111a0c527e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131725" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & -4x+(k-5)y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & k-5 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & k-5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ (k-7)y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"} :step/id #uuid "a93f2400-74e9-5bc9-a239-9a89e32c8532"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b9a3770-af37-58af-91e7-3430fd2463b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343154} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae964-c567-5585-ab23-7241fb114732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343221} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3da90-4b17-5b45-af78-2746f79a0b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343724} {:answer/id #uuid "ad97781e-f202-56a0-803a-f17ee1a49ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343764} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593" :question/math-academy-id "q-74646" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"} :step/id #uuid "b7e356b4-fa42-567c-864c-79ee57dd45e6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492210}]}
